# BDD / self-learning pipeline — three gates

> **Scope**: this rule governs **behave/BDD** asset work **and** explore-first
> writes into `packages/api_objects/**`, `packages/page_objects/**`,
> `assets/design/**`. Auto-attaches on those globs. It is **not** a
> platform-wide default. Task routing lives in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md);
> the BDD **lower half** is orchestrated by
> [`bdd-asset-pipeline`](../agents/bdd-asset-pipeline.md). Explore-first
> learning is specified in `docs/spec/sut-self-learning.md`.

## Framework selection (read first)

- **Default** for UI/API business-flow automation assets is the behave path.
- **Exception — user-explicit pytest**: implement with pytest. Do **not**
  force `.feature` / behave steps / `behave --stage` / these gates.
- When in doubt and the user did **not** name a framework, prefer behave for
  scenario-style UI/API flows.
- Pytest tests should still reuse `tuner_testkit` and this repo's `packages/**`.

## Gate 1 — Evidence is mandatory (explore-first OK)

Any write into `packages/api_objects/**`, `packages/page_objects/**`, or
`assets/design/**` **must** cite at least one `artifacts/evidence/<run_id>/`
record (sanitized). The evidence may come from:

- an **explore session** (no `.feature` yet) via Playwright MCP, or
- a **feature run** via `run-feature-playwright-mcp`.

Do **not** require a pre-existing `.feature` just to satisfy this gate.
Do **not** substitute MCP with local `sync_playwright` solely because UI
steps pass locally.

If capture is blocked (captcha, SSO, OTP, permission prompts, unreachable
env) → **stop**, and report: where it blocked, what human action is needed,
what evidence was collected, what assets can/cannot proceed. Do not write
API/design assets as if capture existed.

## Gate 2 — Freeze API Objects when capture has eligible routes

- If evidence captured **any non-static** route related to the session or
  scenarios, freeze them into `packages/api_objects/**` following
  `freeze-api-objects` (route-aligned, deduped, sanitized).
- If you create zero API Objects, **state why** (pure SPA / all static /
  blocked before login / etc.). Silence is not acceptable.
- Never commit real tokens, cookies, Authorization/Set-Cookie headers, or
  sensitive values — neither in source nor in any evidence bundle.

## Gate 3 — Prove the stages that actually exist

After **behave/BDD** asset changes under `tests/features/`:

- If a UI feature (or UI steps) exist → run `behave --stage ui <feature>`.
- If an API feature (or API steps) exist → run `behave --stage api <feature>`
  (or `--dry-run` with an explicit TODO if the API feature is not yet authored).
- Do **not** fail the task for a stage that has no feature yet.
- For user-explicit **pytest** work, prove with `pytest <path>` instead.

When writing assertions, consult `assets/design/**` first: assert `writes`
tables, skip `noise` tables, use `correlate` / `identity` for locating rows.

## Enforcement summary

- Asset writes are not done unless: sanitized evidence exists under
  `artifacts/evidence/<run_id>/`, eligible routes are frozen (or explicit
  zero-freeze justification), and every **existing** behave stage is exercised.
- User-explicit pytest tasks are done when the requested suite runs
  successfully; do not invent a parallel behave feature unless asked.
- When any applicable gate would be violated, **stop and report the blocker**.
